{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>if his hand has not found enough to restore</b>: meaning, if the Master sees that there is no strength in the people to endure afflictions any longer, and their debts have multiplied beyond measure and their capacity to bear has been exhausted, <b>then his sale shall remain until the Jubilee year</b> — which is the time fixed for redemption in its appointed moment, and then <b>he shall go out in the Jubilee and return to his possession</b>, for the end of the exile exists even if Israel be utterly wicked, God forbid."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:17.312510240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}